pcm: skip voice slots whose key bit is clear  [OPTIONAL - see the numbers]

A slot with its key bit clear produces nothing and remembers nothing. Every
result the loop body computes for it is either discarded or overwritten by the
`if (!active)` clear at the bottom of the loop: ram1[4] is written only when
`active`, ram1[1]/ram1[3]/ram1[5] and ram2[8]/ram2[9]/ram2[10] are zeroed by the
clear, ram2[7] is written only when `key`, and the IRQ is raised only when
`active`. `pan` and `rc` are forced to 0 when !active, so sampl, sampr, rc0 and
rc1 are all exactly 0 and the four accumulator updates collapse to a plain
sx20() of the accumulator.

Two things do still happen and are reproduced: calc_tv<2>() keeps stepping the
filter envelope in ram2[11] -- `write` is unconditionally set by !active, so a
silent slot's filter level keeps moving -- and the chorus/reverb rcadd and
rcadd2 injections are selected by slot position, not by whether the slot is
sounding.

Three exclusions, all found by the differential test rather than by reading:

  * pcm.nfs must be set, because the clear of ram1[1..5] is gated on it;
  * slots 28..31 always take the full path. Their register rows double as the
    mixer and chorus/reverb state -- ram1[28][*] and ram1[29][*] are the reverb
    line's working registers, ram1[30][*] is the DAC stage, ram1[31][1] and
    ram1[31][3] are the mix accumulators -- so the filter's `ram1[1] = v5` and
    `ram1[3] = v1` writes are not dead for them, they clobber shared state the
    next stage reads back;
  * slot nslots-1 always takes the full path, because it stores to
    pcm.accum_l/accum_r rather than back into ram1[31], and its slot2 is 31.
    reg_slots is 1..32, so this is not always slot 31.

WHETHER TO TAKE THIS PATCH IS A JUDGEMENT CALL. It is a large win when voices
are idle and a small loss when they are not, and the loss lands on the case that
decides whether the emulator keeps up. On the ROM-free harness, on top of 0001
to 0005:

  all 32 voices keyed on      27741 -> 28284 Ir/tick   +2.0%   (worst case)
  same, wide pitch spread     28899 -> 29442 Ir/tick   +1.9%
  mixed key traffic           25727 -> 12491 Ir/tick   -51%
  all voices idle             24842 ->  7279 Ir/tick   -71%

The +2% is the extra live range the fast path forces on the main body; it does
not go away with branch hints or a running mask, both of which were tried.

Note also that the sc55d --bench figure for this patch is meaningless: with
placeholder ROMs no voice is ever keyed on, so the benchmark measures nothing
but the fast path.

--- a/src/backend/pcm.cpp
+++ b/src/backend/pcm.cpp
@@ -1093,6 +1093,16 @@
         pcm.rcsum[1] = 0;
 
         const int nslots = pcm.config.reg_slots;
+
+        // Bitmap of the slots whose whole body is dead this tick; see the
+        // fast path inside the loop for why.  Slots 28..31 are excluded because
+        // their register rows are shared with the mixer and the chorus/reverb
+        // line, and slot nslots-1 is excluded because it is the one that writes
+        // the accumulators out to pcm.accum_l / pcm.accum_r.
+        const uint32_t slot_fast = pcm.nfs
+            ? (~voice_active & 0x0fffffffu & ~(1u << (nslots - 1)))
+            : 0u;
+
         for (int slot = 0; slot < nslots; slot++)
         {
             uint32_t *ram1 = pcm.ram1[slot];
@@ -1103,6 +1113,95 @@
             const bool active = okey && key;
             const bool kon = key && !okey;
 
+            // Fast path for a slot whose key bit is clear.
+            //
+            // Everything the main body computes for such a slot is either
+            // discarded or overwritten by the `if (!active)` clear at the bottom
+            // of the loop:
+            //
+            //   ram1[4]                     written only when `active`
+            //   ram1[1], ram1[3], ram1[5]   zeroed by the clear (needs nfs)
+            //   ram2[8], ram2[9], ram2[10]  zeroed by the clear
+            //   ram2[7]                     written only when `key`
+            //   the IRQ                     raised only when `active`
+            //
+            // and `pan` and `rc` are forced to 0 when !active, so sampl, sampr,
+            // rc0 and rc1 are all exactly 0 and the four accumulator updates
+            // degenerate to a plain sx20() of the accumulator.  Two things do
+            // still happen and are reproduced below: calc_tv<2>() keeps stepping
+            // the filter envelope in ram2[11], and the chorus/reverb rcadd and
+            // rcadd2 injections are selected by slot position, not by whether
+            // the slot is sounding.
+            //
+            // `pcm.nfs` is part of the slot_fast condition because the clear of
+            // ram1[1..5] is itself gated on it.  Slots 28..31 are excluded there
+            // too: their register rows double as the mixer and chorus/reverb
+            // state - ram1[28][*] and ram1[29][*] are the reverb line's working
+            // registers, ram1[30][*] is the DAC stage, ram1[31][1] and
+            // ram1[31][3] are the left/right mix accumulators - so for those the
+            // filter's `ram1[1] = v5` and `ram1[3] = v1` writes are not dead at
+            // all, they clobber shared state the next stage reads back.  Slot
+            // nslots-1 is excluded because it stores to pcm.accum_l/accum_r
+            // rather than back into ram1[31], and because its slot2 is 31.
+            //
+            // The body is written out separately rather than as a branch inside
+            // the main path so that the all-voices-active case, which is the one
+            // that decides whether the emulator keeps up, sees exactly the same
+            // code and the same register allocation as before.
+            if ((slot_fast >> slot) & 1)
+            {
+                calc_tv<2>(pcm, taps, ram2[5], &ram2[11], /*active=*/0, NULL);
+
+                // slot2 is slot + 1 here: slot != nslots - 1, and slot < 28,
+                // so case 31 is unreachable.  Same single mask test and merged
+                // switch as the main path uses.
+                if ((0x00e60000u >> (slot + 1)) & 1)
+                {
+                    switch (slot + 1)
+                    {
+                        case 17:
+                            pcm.ram1[31][1] = (uint32_t)addclip20((int32_t)pcm.ram1[31][1], rcadd[0] >> 1, rcadd[0] & 1);
+                            pcm.rcsum[1] = addclip20(pcm.rcsum[1], rcadd2[0] >> 1, rcadd2[0] & 1);
+                            break;
+                        case 18:
+                            pcm.ram1[31][3] = (uint32_t)addclip20((int32_t)pcm.ram1[31][3], rcadd[1] >> 1, rcadd[1] & 1);
+                            pcm.rcsum[1] = addclip20(pcm.rcsum[1], rcadd2[1] >> 1, rcadd2[1] & 1);
+                            break;
+                        case 21:
+                            pcm.ram1[31][1] = (uint32_t)addclip20((int32_t)pcm.ram1[31][1], rcadd[2] >> 1, rcadd[2] & 1);
+                            pcm.rcsum[0] = addclip20(pcm.rcsum[0], rcadd2[2] >> 1, rcadd2[2] & 1);
+                            break;
+                        case 22:
+                            pcm.ram1[31][3] = (uint32_t)addclip20((int32_t)pcm.ram1[31][3], rcadd[3] >> 1, rcadd[3] & 1);
+                            pcm.rcsum[1] = addclip20(pcm.rcsum[1], rcadd2[3] >> 1, rcadd2[3] & 1);
+                            break;
+                        case 23:
+                            pcm.ram1[31][1] = (uint32_t)addclip20((int32_t)pcm.ram1[31][1], rcadd[4] >> 1, rcadd[4] & 1);
+                            pcm.rcsum[0] = addclip20(pcm.rcsum[0], rcadd2[4] >> 1, rcadd2[4] & 1);
+                            break;
+                    }
+                }
+
+                // addclip20(acc, 0, 0) == sx20(acc)
+                const int32_t suml = sx20((int32_t)pcm.ram1[31][1]);
+                const int32_t sumr = sx20((int32_t)pcm.ram1[31][3]);
+
+                pcm.rcsum[0] = sx20(pcm.rcsum[0]);
+                pcm.rcsum[1] = sx20(pcm.rcsum[1]);
+
+                // slot != nslots - 1, so the accumulators stay in ram1[31]
+                pcm.ram1[31][1] = (uint32_t)suml;
+                pcm.ram1[31][3] = (uint32_t)sumr;
+
+                ram1[1] = 0;
+                ram1[3] = 0;
+                ram1[5] = 0;
+                ram2[8] = 0;
+                ram2[9] = 0;
+                ram2[10] = 0;
+                continue;
+            }
+
             // address generator
 
             bool b15 = (ram2[8] & 0x8000) != 0; // 0
